    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q_apply": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I apply them?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>1. Prep properly.</strong> Push back your cuticles with the stick, lightly buff the surface with the file, and wipe each nail with the alcohol pad. This step is boring and it is also the whole ballgame — 90% of “they fell off in two days” traces straight back to skipping it.</p><p><strong>2. Size them out first.</strong> Lay all ten nails against your fingers and match each one before any adhesive comes out. Once glue is involved, there’s no rearranging.</p><p><strong>3. Apply.</strong> Tabs for a gentler, reusable wear; glue for the long haul. Press from the cuticle down and hold firmly for 30 seconds.</p><p><strong>4. Give it an hour</strong> before water.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_reuse": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are they reusable?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — and we’d love you to. Applied with tabs and removed patiently, a set can be worn again and again. Glue gives you a longer wear but is harder on the nail coming off, so if reuse matters most to you, tabs are your friend.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_damage": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will they damage my natural nails?",
            "answer": "<p>Not when they’re removed the right way. No drilling, no acetone soak, no filing down your natural nail. The damage people blame on press-ons almost always comes from impatience at removal — so please don’t pry.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_remove": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I take them off without wrecking my nails?",
            "answer": "<p>Soak your fingertips in warm soapy water with a few drops of oil for 10–15 minutes, then ease each nail up gently from the side with the cuticle stick. If it resists, it isn’t ready — soak longer. Never pull. The nail will come off either way; the only question is whether it takes a layer of you with it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_popped": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "One popped off. Is the set ruined?",
            "answer": "<p>Not at all. Clean off the old adhesive, re-prep the nail, and re-apply — you’ve got spare tabs in the kit. This is the quiet advantage of press-ons over acrylics: a bad day is a five-minute fix, not a salon appointment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_handmade": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My set has slight variations from the photo. Is it faulty?",
            "answer": "<p>Almost certainly not. Hand-painted work carries small differences in tone, placement and finish from set to set — that’s the signature of something made by a person rather than a machine. Genuine defects (lifting embellishments, cracks, rough edges) are a different matter, and we’ll always make those right.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_wrong": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Something’s not right with my order. What can you do?",
            "answer": "<p>Tell us and we’ll take care of it. If your set arrives damaged, faulty, or simply isn’t what you ordered, email <strong>hello@urbanstudionails.com within 7 days of delivery</strong> with your order number and a couple of clear photos. We’ll make it right — a replacement, a partial refund, or a full refund, whichever genuinely fits the situation.</p><p>And in most cases you won’t need to post anything back to us. Good photos are enough.</p><p>The one thing we’re not able to do is take a set back because it wasn’t quite what you’d pictured — a size that doesn’t fit, or a shade that looked different on your screen. Nails are worn directly on the body, so like most beauty and personal care products, they can’t be resold once they’ve left us.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_shipping": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "When will my order ship?",
            "answer": "<p>Every set on our site is in stock and ready to ship. Most orders leave us within 24 hours, Monday to Friday. During launches, holidays or exceptionally busy weeks, please allow up to 3–5 business days. Either way, you’ll get a tracking number the moment yours is on its way.</p><p>The one exception is Custom Couture — those are made from scratch to your design, so allow 5–20 business days before dispatch.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
